meta {
  name: List Alert Rules
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/alerts
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt_token}}
}

docs {
  List every alert rule (enabled or not).

  Each rule:
    { id, name, description, enabled, expression, severity,
      for_duration_secs, eval_interval_secs, cooldown_secs,
      created_at, updated_at }

  Expression grammar:
    `<ns>.<field>{<labels>} <cmp> <number>`
    namespaces: cpu | memory | disk | network | pressure | components
                | probe | service
    comparators: > >= < <= == !=

  Examples:
    cpu.usage_percent > 80
    memory.swap_in_pages_per_sec > 0
    disk.used_bytes{mount_point="/"} > 1073741824
    pressure.some_avg10{resource="memory"} > 5.0
    probe.free_pct{probe_name="disk-free-root"} < 10
    service.up{unit="nginx.service"} == 0

  The `service` namespace is a live OS lookup, not a time-series read.
  The `unit` label is mandatory. See /alerts/schema for the full
  catalogue.
}
